(Send signal <N> to process <pid>. performs kill(2). A parent forks a
 child that waits; the parent sends SIGKILL (9) to the child pid, then
 reaps. The reaped pid must match the forked child pid - proving a
 SIGKILLed child is delivered and reapable. The kill arrives
 immediately, so the child's long Wait is interrupted and the test
 completes fast; it never actually sleeps 30 seconds.)

Set pid to fork the process.
If pid is 0 then,
    Wait 30 seconds.
If pid is greater than 0 then,
    Send signal 9 to process pid.
    Set reaped to reap any child process.
    If reaped is pid then,
        Print "sigkilled child reaped with matching pid".